# Updating the PacketFence fork

This document describes how to update the inverse-inc/Akamai (PacketFence) fork of FreeRADIUS to a newer upstream release.

## Get the latest source

## Starting from scratch (fresh clone)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server
cd freeradius-server
git remote add inverse-inc https://github.com/inverse-inc/freeradius-server
git fetch --all
```

## From an existing clone

```bash
cd <PATH_TO_REPO>
git fetch --all
```

## Update to a new upstream version

Assume the new upstream release is `3.2.8` and the current PacketFence branch is based on `3.2.7`.


Create a new branch for the new PacketFence version (based on the new upstream release branch/tag):

```bash
git checkout -B feature/PacketFence_3.2.8 release_3_2_8
```

Cherry-pick the PacketFence-specific commits from the previous version onto the new branch:

```bash
git cherry-pick release_3_2_7..feature/PacketFence_3.2.7
```

Notes:
- If the previous PacketFence branch contains merge commits, `git cherry-pick` may ask for a mainline parent; in that case, use `git cherry-pick -m <parent>` for the specific merge commit(s) as needed.
- Replace version numbers/branch names to match the upstream naming used in this repo (e.g. tags vs release branches).

After resolving conflicts and validating the build/tests, push the new branch:

```bash
git push -u inverse-inc feature/PacketFence_3.2.8
```

## Building packages

An internal build server is available with scripts to build packages for RHEL 8 and Debian 12.

Connect using SSH (internal):

```bash
ssh <username>@hq.inverse.ca -p 2222
```

If your key is already authorized on the build server, direct access may also work (internal IP): `172.105.106.229`.


### RHEL

Once connected, go to `/root/build` and edit `Dockerfile` to change the GitHub branch you want to build:

```Dockerfile
ARG release=feature/PacketFence_3.2.8
```

Then build the container:

```bash
docker build . --build-arg ssh_prv_key="$(cat ./id_rsa)" --build-arg ssh_pub_key="$(cat ./id_rsa.pub)" --no-cache -t freeradius-3.2.8
```

If the compilation succeeds, the packages will be available in `/home/rsync/rpm/release/`.

### Debian

Once connected, go to `/root/builddebian` and edit `Dockerfile` to change the GitHub branch you want to build:

```Dockerfile
ARG release=feature/PacketFence_3.2.8
```

Then build the container:

```bash
docker build . --build-arg ssh_prv_key="$(cat ./id_rsa)" --build-arg ssh_pub_key="$(cat ./id_rsa.pub)" --no-cache -t freeradius-3.2.8
```

If the compilation succeeds, the packages will be available in `/home/rsync/debian/release/`.
